UPDATE dbo.fact_vacantes SET titulo=N'UX Researcher — Audience and Product Experience Research', descripcion=N'<h3>Perfil</h3><p><strong>Note on Communication:</strong> Excellent spoken and written English is essential. You will independently conduct in-depth interviews with American customers. You must be able to build rapport, pick up on nuance, ask neutral follow-up questions, and communicate findings clearly and concisely.</p><p>WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</p><ul><li>Proven experience independently planning and executing end-to-end UX research that directly influenced product decisions and business outcomes.</li><li>Strong portfolio or case studies demonstrating your personal, hands-on contribution across generative and evaluative studies.</li><li>Mastery of in-depth customer interviewing, neutral moderation, switch interviews, and usability testing.</li><li>Deep practical experience with frameworks such as Jobs to Be Done (JTBD) and Strategyzer (Value Proposition Canvas, Test/Learning Cards).</li><li>BIG BENEFIT: Analyst background or experience with product analytics tools (e.g. Mixpanel, Clarity, Google Analytics etc)</li><li>Exceptional listening and communication skills; adept at presenting actionable insights to executive leadership and mentoring junior teammates.</li><li>AI-proeficient but not AI-dependent</li></ul><h3>Funciones</h3><p><strong>1. Clarify Our Product Portfolio &amp; Customer Value</strong></p><ul><li>Investigate who our products serve, the circumstances in which people use them, their Jobs to Be Done (JTBD), alternatives, unmet needs, and desired outcomes.</li><li>Evaluate and refine existing customer segments and personas as new evidence emerges.</li><li>Distinguish the reasons people initially subscribe from the value they experience through sustained, habitual use.</li><li>Investigate acquisition, engagement, retention, and cancellation journeys to pinpoint where perceived value declines and what ultimately causes churn.</li><li>Plan and conduct customer interviews, JTBD switch interviews, direct observation, and targeted surveys.</li><li>Work with internal teams to screen, recruit, and schedule participants (including new, active, lapsed, and former subscribers, as well as prospective readers).</li><li>Produce evidence-backed customer profiles, JTBD findings, journey maps, and Strategyzer Value Proposition Canvases to identify gaps, overlaps, and strategic priorities across our portfolio.</li></ul><p><strong>2. Define Success &amp; Goals</strong></p><ul><li>Help Product and Analytics define success from the customer''s perspective: whether people accomplish their job, experience clear value, or encounter friction.</li><li>Combine qualitative feedback with quantitative measures in product and membership scorecards.</li><li>Help establish baseline metrics, define research measures, and inform targets.</li></ul><p><strong>3. Establish a Continuous Improvement Cycle</strong></p><ul><li>Turn findings into testable hypotheses and help prioritize research and experimentation backlogs.</li><li>Conduct concept, prototype, and usability tests; evaluate customer experience before and after release.</li><li>Align on success criteria prior to testing.</li><li>Use Strategyzer Test Cards and Learning Cards to document assumptions, methods, observations, and next steps.</li><li>Share objective findings that support, challenge, or overturn proposals—recommending whether to expand, pivot, stop, or investigate further.</li></ul><h3>Deseable</h3><p>MixpanelMixpanel, Clarity, Google Analytics </p><h3>Beneficios</h3><p>Remote-friendly.<br>Competitive pay.<br>Mission-driven company.</p>' WHERE url_vacante=N'https://www.getonbrd.com/jobs/ux-researcher-audience-and-product-experience-research-epoch-times-remote' AND fuente_id IN (SELECT fuente_id FROM dbo.dim_fuente WHERE nombre='GetOnBoard');
