UPDATE dbo.fact_vacantes SET titulo=N'Back-end Software Engineer', descripcion=N'<h3>What we’re looking for</h3><p>For us, Senior isn’t a matter of years or of how many technologies you know. It’s how you work:</p><ul><li>You understand the problem before you solve it. You ask what the business or user actually needs, and sometimes the right answer is not to build anything.</li><li>You choose the simplest solution that works.</li><li>To you, complexity is a cost.</li><li>You make trade-offs explicit and explain your reasoning.</li><li>You own outcomes, not tasks.</li><li>You surface risks early, say when a plan is no longer realistic, and see things through after release.</li><li>You build things others can maintain.</li><li>Your code is clear, tested and easy to evolve without you in the room.</li><li>You think about what can go wrong. Failing dependencies, bad data, security and performance are part of the design, not an afterthought.</li><li>You act like a consultant.</li><li>You adapt how you communicate to engineers, product and clients, and you bring recommendations, not only problems.</li><li>You make your team better. You give thoughtful reviews, share what you know and help others grow, without becoming a bottleneck.</li><li>You keep learning. You get productive in unfamiliar systems and know when to ask for help.</li><li>You use AI responsibly. It makes you faster, but you understand and validate everything before it ships.</li></ul><ul><li>4+ years building backends with Python and Django (Django REST Framework a big plus)</li><li>Solid experience with PostgreSQL in production, including schema changes on live systems</li><li>Hands-on experience with background processing (Celery, RabbitMQ, Redis or similar)</li><li>You’ve built and maintained integrations with third-party APIs and know what happens when they fail</li><li>You care about testing, code quality and constructive code reviews</li><li>You’ve supported your own work in production: monitoring, debugging and incidents don’t scare you</li><li>You’re comfortable in a large codebase shared with many engineers</li><li>C1 English: you’ll work daily with a US-based team, in meetings and in writing</li></ul><h3>Funciones</h3><ul><li>Build product features end to end on the backend, from the API to the database</li><li>Connect the platform with hotel suppliers, booking systems, payment providers and AI services, and keep those connections reliable when the other side isn’t</li><li>Design and run the background jobs that keep bookings, payments and data in sync</li><li>Evolve the database of a live product without interrupting the people who rely on it</li><li>Write short technical proposals before big changes, and review your teammates’ work</li><li>Take your turn on call, help resolve production issues, and leave things better than you found them</li></ul><h3>Deseable</h3><ul><li>Experience in the travel industry (hotels, airlines, cruises, booking systems)</li><li>Experience with payments or financial flows (Stripe, invoicing, payouts)</li><li>You’ve shipped AI-powered features to real users</li><li>Familiarity with Docker, Kubernetes or AWS</li></ul><h3>Beneficios</h3>' WHERE url_vacante=N'https://www.getonbrd.com/jobs/backend-software-engineer-zaelot-remote-fbc2' AND fuente_id IN (SELECT fuente_id FROM dbo.dim_fuente WHERE nombre='GetOnBoard');
