UPDATE dbo.fact_vacantes SET titulo=N'Data Architect (Microsoft Fabric)', descripcion=N'<h3>QUALIFICATIONS</h3><ul><li>8+ years of total technical experience in data engineering, analytics, or enterprise data platforms, including 3+ years in a dedicated data architecture or technical lead role.</li><li>Strong understanding of modern data architecture patterns, including Lakehouse, data warehouse, dimensional modeling, and semantic modeling.</li><li>Experience with cloud data platforms, preferably Microsoft Azure and Microsoft Fabric.</li><li>Working knowledge of Power BI architecture and data governance concepts, including metadata, lineage, security, and compliance.</li><li>Strong communication and stakeholder management skills, with the ability to translate business strategy into architecture roadmaps.</li><li>Advanced English proficiency, written and spoken, required for daily collaboration with U.S.-based teams and client-facing engagements.</li><li>Valid passport and up-to-date travel documentation for the United States, as occasional international travel may be required depending on client and project needs.</li></ul><h3>Funciones</h3><ul><li>Define enterprise data architecture standards, reference architectures, and implementation patterns for Microsoft Fabric, Power BI, Purview, and Azure-based data platforms.</li><li>Lead the design of Fabric-first analytics architectures, including OneLake strategy, Lakehouse and Warehouse patterns, workspace structure, domains, capacity considerations, and data product design.</li><li>Establish Power BI architecture standards for semantic models, certified datasets, deployment pipelines, workspace governance, performance optimization, and self-service reporting.</li><li>Define Microsoft Purview governance models including data catalog standards, lineage, business glossary, classification, ownership, stewardship, metadata management, and information protection alignment practices.</li><li>Guide modernization from legacy databases, data warehouses, reporting platforms, and fragmented data stores into governed lakehouse and analytics ecosystems.</li><li>Design integration strategies across cloud, on-premises, SaaS, operational systems, APIs, data warehouses, and analytics platforms.</li><li>Define data security, access control, privacy, retention, quality, and compliance patterns aligned to client and regulatory requirements.</li><li>Partner with executive stakeholders, business leaders, delivery teams, and technical specialists to align data architecture with strategic outcomes.</li><li>Conduct architecture reviews, solution assessments, platform readiness evaluations, and roadmap planning sessions.</li><li>Translate complex Fabric architectures and data solutions into clear, business-friendly explanations for both technical and non-technical audiences.</li><li>Document data architectures, pipelines, and technical decisions.</li><li>Mentor data engineers, BI developers, analysts, and client teams on architecture standards and best practices.</li></ul><h3>Deseable</h3><ul><li>Experience designing analytics platforms for enterprise reporting and self-service BI.</li><li>Deep expertise in Power BI semantic models, governance, performance, and deployment lifecycle.</li><li>Strong data governance skills: metadata, lineage, classification, security, and compliance.</li><li>Experience leading architecture workshops, technical discovery, and modernization planning.</li><li>Hands-on experience with Fabric architecture: OneLake, Lakehouse, Warehouse, Data Factory, workspaces, security, and capacity planning.</li><li>Experience leading Microsoft Purview adoption or a Power BI Center of Excellence, including catalog, lineage, glossary, or reporting operating models.</li><li>Experience with Azure Data Lake, Azure SQL, Data Factory, Synapse, Databricks, Delta Lake, or enterprise integration tools.</li><li>Experience supporting AI and Copilot readiness, responsible data usage, and analytics modernization.</li><li>Fabric, Power BI, Azure Solutions Architect, Azure Data Engineer, or governance certifications are a plus.</li></ul><h3>Beneficios</h3><ul><li>Competitive salary.</li><li>Opportunity to lead Fabric, Power BI, Purview, and AI-readiness strategy for Integratz''s enterprise data warehouse modernization program.</li><li>Ownership of a named, repeatable architecture method, applied end-to-end on this engagement rather than a one-off design task.</li><li>High-impact consulting role influencing modernization, analytics operating models, and executive data strategy.</li><li>Flexible, primarily remote work environment.</li><li>Collaborative, inclusive, multicultural team culture, with opportunities to mentor engineers and shape Integratz''s data practice.</li><li>Growth path into principal architecture, data strategy, governance, or analytics advisory roles, with access to certifications and cutting-edge tools.</li></ul>' WHERE url_vacante=N'https://www.getonbrd.com/jobs/data-architect-microsoft-fabric-integratz-vina-del-mar-8c2e' AND fuente_id IN (SELECT fuente_id FROM dbo.dim_fuente WHERE nombre='GetOnBoard');
