UPDATE dbo.fact_vacantes SET titulo=N'Senior Software Engineer', descripcion=N'<h3>What we''re looking for</h3><ul><li>5+ years building production web applications, with real ownership of systems on both frontend and backend.</li><li>Strong TypeScript, Next.js, Prisma and Postgres. You understand the server/client boundary, caching, and how schema and query design affect the product.</li><li>You work with AI agents as a lead, not a typist. You run several agents on real work, know where they fail, and catch what they get wrong before it ships.</li><li>You''ve improved an agent harness at your current job: better context, tools, rules, review loops or evals that measurably changed agent output. Tell us what you changed and what it fixed.</li><li>You''re curious about how your role is changing with AI, and you have opinions about it.</li><li>You''re comfortable with non-technical stakeholders. You can ask the right questions, push back on the wrong solution and explain trade-offs in plain language.</li><li>Good technical taste: you prefer simple, boring solutions and delete code as readily as you write it.</li><li>Professional English for daily written and spoken work.</li></ul><h3>Funciones</h3><ul><li>Work directly with PMs and the company''s departments to understand their problems, then turn them into scoped, shippable solutions.</li><li>Build features across the stack: Next.js (App Router, Server Components, Server Actions), Prisma and Postgres.</li><li>Orchestrate several AI coding agents in parallel. Break work down, write the specs and context they need, review their output critically and own the result.</li><li>Improve our agent harness: the prompts, tools, context, guardrails and evals that make agents reliable on our codebase.</li><li>Design the contracts between frontend and backend, and keep them stable as the product evolves.</li><li>Review code, human or AI-written, with a focus on authorization, data integrity, payments and privacy.</li><li>Help shape how our engineering team works as AI changes what an engineer''s day looks like.</li></ul><h3>Deseable</h3><ul><li>Infrastructure experience isn''t required, but it helps.</li><li>Google Cloud (Cloud Run, Cloud SQL, IAM, Secret Manager) or comparable AWS experience.</li><li>Experience in regulated or privacy-sensitive domains: health, legal, insurance or government benefits.</li></ul><h3>Beneficios</h3><p>15 PTO days + your country holidays + Sick days </p><p>Good communication is non-negotiable for us. We love communication, and we dislike meetings that could have been a Slack message.</p><ul><li><strong>Async first.</strong> Most of our work happens in writing. When async isn''t enough, we jump on a quick huddle instead of letting a thread drag on.</li><li><strong>Share progress often.</strong> Post updates, blockers and decisions without being asked. If we have to ask how things are going, that''s a bad sign.</li><li><strong>Write clearly.</strong> Your messages should give the reader enough context to act without a follow-up question.</li></ul>' WHERE url_vacante=N'https://www.getonbrd.com/jobs/senior-software-engineer-vetclaims-ai-remote' AND fuente_id IN (SELECT fuente_id FROM dbo.dim_fuente WHERE nombre='GetOnBoard');
DELETE e FROM dbo.cert_evidencia_v2 e JOIN dbo.fact_vacantes v ON v.vacante_id=e.vacante_id WHERE url_vacante=N'https://www.getonbrd.com/jobs/senior-software-engineer-vetclaims-ai-remote' AND fuente_id IN (SELECT fuente_id FROM dbo.dim_fuente WHERE nombre='GetOnBoard');
UPDATE dbo.fact_vacantes SET titulo=N'Senior Cloud Engineer', descripcion=N'<h3>Qualifications</h3><div><strong>Key Competencies</strong></div><ul><li><strong>Ability to Multitask. </strong>Demonstrates strong technical and operational agility, effectively navigating complex business and cloud environments to deliver tailored, high-quality support across WWF’s Azure and multi-cloud platforms.</li><li><strong>Solution-Oriented and Strategic Collaboration. </strong>Clear, influential communicator who leads projects end-to-end, ensuring alignment, transparency, and active engagement with stakeholders across technical and non-technical teams.</li><li><strong>Growth Mindset. </strong>Demonstrates a strong growth mindset, continually expanding expertise in evolving cloud, automation, and security technologies and applying new knowledge to strengthen WWF’s technical capabilities.</li><li><strong>Big Picture Thinking</strong>. Strategic acumen complemented by robust technical proficiency Collaborative.</li><li><strong>Collaborative.</strong> Proven ability to work effectively as part of a team </li><li><strong>Project Management.</strong> Strong organizational, documentation, and project management capabilities, including development of comprehensive project plans</li></ul><div><strong>Skills and Abilities</strong></div><ul><li>Degree in IT or related field AND minimum of 8 years of work experience (including at least 6 years of experience in IT)</li><li>MUST HAVE Verbal and written fluency in English and Spanish</li><li>Experience managing large-scale enterprise IT systems</li><li>Extensive hands-on experience managing highly available and resilient Azure production systems.</li><li>In-depth knowledge of Microsoft Azure services, cloud architecture, cloud networking, Entra ID, Microsoft 365, and Windows and Linux servers</li><li>Proficient in managing Windows domains and Active Directory</li><li>Expertise in using PowerShell and Graph API for Azure management, workflow automation, and deployment orchestration</li><li>Familiarity with provisioning and managing access for technologies such as Fabric, Power BI, and Azure Foundry</li><li>Experience integrating Microsoft Copilot for M365, Copilot Studio, and Copilot Agents into enterprise Azure/M365 environments, including configuration and governance of data access controls</li><li>Significant expertise in building, deploying, and managing virtual machines in Azure from inception</li><li>History of applying structured thinking to diagnose complex cloud or hybrid system issues and develop scalable, sustainable solutions.</li><li>Well-honed methodologies for diagnosing and troubleshooting technical issues.</li><li>Broad enterprise scale expertise across infrastructure, Azure cloud architecture, identity and access management with Entra ID, and emerging AI‐ driven‐ automation technologies—enabling the evaluation and recommendation of modernization opportunities, security improvements, and strategic technology replacements. </li><li>Skills in configuring Microsoft Entra tenants and domains, including DNS and VNET setup.</li><li>Committed to building and strengthening a culture of inclusion within and across teams.</li><li>Identifies and aligns with WWF’s core values:<ul><li>COURAGE – We demonstrate courage through our actions, we work for change where it’s needed, and we inspire people and institutions to tackle the greatest threats to nature and the future of the planet, which is our home.</li><li>INTEGRITY – We live the principles we call on others to meet. We act with integrity, accountability and transparency, and we rely on facts and science to guide us and to ensure that we learn and evolve.</li><li>RESPECT – We honor the voices and knowledge of people and communities that we serve, and we work to secure their rights to a sustainable future. </li><li>COLLABORATION – We deliver impact at the scale of the challenges we face through the power of collective action and innovation.</li></ul></li></ul><h3>Funciones</h3><div><strong>Own Our Azure Infrastructure</strong></div><ul><li>You''ll be the architect behind WWF''s Azure environment, spinning up subscriptions, provisioning resources, and building/deploying VMs (Windows, SQL, Red Hat, firewalls) from the ground up in both production and staging.</li></ul><div><strong>Lock Down Security &amp; Identity</strong></div><ul><li>Configure Microsoft Entra tenants, manage SSO through Azure Enterprise Apps, and keep our RBAC and user groups clean and secure.</li><li>You''ll patch systems proactively and use PowerShell + Graph API to automate the boring stuff so the important stuff runs smoother.</li></ul><div><strong>Be Our Safety Net</strong></div><ul><li>Design backup strategies and disaster recovery playbooks that actually work when it matters.</li><li>You''re the reason we sleep at night knowing our systems can bounce back from anything.</li></ul><div><strong>Keep Everything Connected</strong></div><ul><li>Troubleshoot networking across VNETs, sites, and tenants.</li><li>Firewalls, load balancers, DNS (Azure + Cloudflare), you speak the language fluently and fix problems before they become fires.</li></ul><div><strong>Be the Go-To Expert</strong></div><ul><li>When Azure, Entra ID, or M365 issues get complicated, you''re who the team calls.</li><li>You''ll lead projects end-to-end and keep stakeholders, technical and non-technical alike, in the loop every step of the way.</li></ul><div><strong>Show Up When It Counts</strong></div><ul><li>Occasional after-hours or weekend work for critical outages or planned maintenance, because uptime matters, and so does the team that protects it.</li></ul><h3>Deseable</h3><h3>Beneficios</h3><p><strong>Remuneration:</strong> Salary and benefits for this position will be paid in local currency.<br><strong>Please note: </strong>Candidates must be currently based and authorized to work in Mexico </p>' WHERE url_vacante=N'https://www.getonbrd.com/jobs/senior-cloud-engineer-world-wildlife-fund-inc-remote' AND fuente_id IN (SELECT fuente_id FROM dbo.dim_fuente WHERE nombre='GetOnBoard');
