UPDATE dbo.fact_vacantes SET titulo=N'Msp Senior System Engineer', descripcion=N'<h3>Qualifications and requirements</h3><ul><li>At least five years of continuous professional IT experience.</li><li>At least one year of experience working in a managed service provider (MSP) environment.</li><li>Strong working knowledge of networking, including firewalls, VLANs, VPNs, routing, and switching.</li><li>Hands-on experience administering Windows Server and Microsoft 365 environments.</li><li>Experience with Microsoft Entra ID, Exchange Online, Intune or other mobile/device management platforms, and endpoint management.</li><li>Experience using remote monitoring and management (RMM) and professional services automation (PSA) platforms.</li><li>Practical understanding of cybersecurity fundamentals, including identity and access control, endpoint protection, patching, and secure system configuration.</li><li>Strong troubleshooting and problem-solving skills across multiple client environments.</li><li>Ability to manage priorities, work independently, and take ownership of assigned issues and projects.</li><li>Clear written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to explain technical issues to clients.</li></ul><h3>Funciones</h3><p><strong>Technical Escalation and Troubleshooting</strong></p><ul><li>Serve as the senior escalation point for issues frontline technicians cannot resolve.</li><li>Troubleshoot complex problems across networks, servers, endpoints, identity, and cloud environments.</li><li>Identify root causes and implement lasting solutions.</li><li>Use sound judgment during high-impact incidents and service disruptions.</li></ul><p><strong>Project Engineering and Infrastructure</strong></p><ul><li>Lead client projects, including migrations, deployments, upgrades, and system improvements.</li><li>Configure systems for reliability, performance, and security.</li><li>Plan changes to minimize disruption.</li><li>Document configurations, projects, and resolutions.</li></ul><p><strong>Security and Best Practices</strong></p><ul><li>Apply security best practices when configuring and troubleshooting client environments.</li><li>Understand identity and access controls, endpoint protection, patch management, and security risks.</li><li>Identify suspicious activity and weaknesses, escalating concerns as needed.</li><li>Support client security and compliance requirements.</li></ul><p><strong>Client Communication and Service Delivery</strong></p><ul><li>Communicate technical issues, project progress, risks, and solutions to clients.</li><li>Explain complex concepts clearly to technical and non-technical audiences.</li><li>Set expectations and provide timely updates.</li><li>Document work accurately and communicate outcomes.</li></ul><p><strong>Teamwork and Continuous Improvement</strong></p><ul><li>Work independently while keeping the team informed.</li><li>Collaborate with technicians and engineers to resolve escalations and improve service.</li><li>Share knowledge and promote consistent troubleshooting and documentation.</li><li>Recommend improvements to processes, standards, and efficiency.</li></ul><h3>Deseable</h3><ul><li>Experience supporting clients in regulated industries, such as defense contracting, financial services, or insurance.</li><li>Familiarity with compliance frameworks and requirements, including CMMC, NIST SP 800-171, GLBA, or the FTC Safeguards Rule.</li><li>Relevant certifications in Microsoft, CompTIA, Cisco, or Meraki technologies.</li><li>Experience leading complex migrations, infrastructure upgrades, or other client engineering projects.</li><li>Experience with security monitoring, endpoint detection and response (EDR), application control, or identity security solutions.</li><li>Experience with scripting, automation, and technical standardization initiatives.</li></ul><h3>Beneficios</h3><ul><li>Resolves complex escalations independently and knows when to involve others.</li><li>Delivers reliable, secure technical solutions that address root causes rather than temporary symptoms.</li><li>Completes client projects with clear documentation and minimal operational disruption.</li><li>Communicates proactively and builds trust with clients and colleagues.</li><li>Takes ownership of technical issues, follows through on commitments, and contributes to continuous improvement.</li></ul>' WHERE url_vacante=N'https://www.getonbrd.com/jobs/msp-senior-system-engineer-pacific-cloud-cyber-remote' AND fuente_id IN (SELECT fuente_id FROM dbo.dim_fuente WHERE nombre='GetOnBoard');
DELETE e FROM dbo.cert_evidencia_v2 e JOIN dbo.fact_vacantes v ON v.vacante_id=e.vacante_id WHERE url_vacante=N'https://www.getonbrd.com/jobs/msp-senior-system-engineer-pacific-cloud-cyber-remote' AND fuente_id IN (SELECT fuente_id FROM dbo.dim_fuente WHERE nombre='GetOnBoard');
UPDATE dbo.fact_vacantes SET titulo=N'AI / ML Engineer', descripcion=N'<h3>What we are looking for</h3><ul><li><strong>Strong Python development experience.</strong></li><li><strong>Experience working with Qwen or similar open-source LLMs.</strong></li><li><strong>Experience building and/or tuning LLMs and GenAI applications.</strong></li><li><strong>Strong software engineering and integration skills.</strong></li><li><strong>Ability to collaborate</strong> across data science and engineering and translate ideas into production-ready implementations.</li><li><strong>Comfort working end-to-end</strong>, from experimentation to production delivery.</li><li><strong>Experience developing GenAI features and working with modern AI tooling.</strong></li></ul><p>We value clear communication, practical problem-solving, and a collaborative approach—because we build long-term, measurable outcomes together.</p><h3>Funciones</h3><p>We’re looking for a GenAI / ML Engineer who can bridge the gap between data science and software engineering. We’ll have you working hands-on with open-source LLMs, building GenAI capabilities, and integrating them into internal tools and applications.</p><ul><li>Build and develop LLM-powered applications and GenAI features.</li><li>Work hands-on with open-source models (including Qwen), including tuning and customization.</li><li>Develop internal tools and capabilities around LLMs.</li><li>Integrate AI/ML capabilities into existing applications and systems (not only greenfield development).</li><li>Partner across data science and engineering to take ideas from experimentation through production.</li><li>Use tools such as Claude Code to accelerate development and delivery.</li></ul><h3>Deseable</h3><ul><li>Experience with additional open-source LLMs beyond Qwen.</li><li>Hands-on familiarity with modern AI tooling and accelerators for GenAI development (e.g., Claude Code or similar developer tools).</li><li>Track record of integrating model-driven features into production systems and internal applications.</li><li>Comfort iterating quickly during experimentation while maintaining software engineering best practices.</li></ul><h3>Beneficios</h3><ul><li>Contrato a largo plazo.</li><li>100% Remoto.</li><li>Vacaciones y PTOs.</li><li>Posibilidad de recibir 2 bonos al año.</li><li>2 revisiones salariales al año.</li><li>Clases de inglés.</li><li>Equipamiento Apple.</li><li>Plataforma de cursos en línea.</li><li>Budget para compra de libros.</li><li>Budget para compra de materiales de trabajo.</li><li>Mucho más..</li></ul>' WHERE url_vacante=N'https://www.getonbrd.com/jobs/ai-ml-engineer-improving-remote' AND fuente_id IN (SELECT fuente_id FROM dbo.dim_fuente WHERE nombre='GetOnBoard');
DELETE e FROM dbo.cert_evidencia_v2 e JOIN dbo.fact_vacantes v ON v.vacante_id=e.vacante_id WHERE url_vacante=N'https://www.getonbrd.com/jobs/ai-ml-engineer-improving-remote' AND fuente_id IN (SELECT fuente_id FROM dbo.dim_fuente WHERE nombre='GetOnBoard');
UPDATE dbo.fact_vacantes SET titulo=N'DevOps Engineer', descripcion=N'<h3>Calificaciones clave</h3><ul><li>Estudios de Ingeniería Civil en Computación o similar.</li><li>Experiencia práctica de al menos 3 años en ingeniería de software o sistemas (DevOps, SRE, ML Engineer).</li><li>Experiencia con Python.</li><li>Pasión en problemáticas de infraestructura y producción.</li><li>Experiencia con servidores cloud (GCP, AWS o Azure), especialmente el conjunto de servicios de procesamiento de datos.</li><li>Experiencia en Infrastructure as code, observabilidad y monitoreo.</li><li>Experiencia en pipelines de CI/CD y Docker</li><li>Habilidad para debug, optimizar código y automatizar tareas rutinarias.</li><li>Buen manejo de inglés, sobre todo en lectura donde debes ser capaz de leer un paper, artículos o documentación de forma constante.</li><li>Habilidades de comunicación y trabajo colaborativo.</li></ul><p>¡En NeuralWorks nos importa la diversidad! Creemos firmemente en la creación de un ambiente laboral inclusivo, diverso y equitativo. Reconocemos y celebramos la diversidad en todas sus formas y estamos comprometidos a ofrecer igualdad de oportunidades para todos los candidatos.</p><p>“Los hombres postulan a un cargo cuando cumplen el 60% de las calificaciones, pero las mujeres sólo si cumplen el 100%.” D. Gaucher , J. Friesen and A. C. Kay, Journal of Personality and Social Psychology, 2011.</p><p>Te invitamos a postular aunque no cumplas con todos los requisitos.</p><h3>Funciones</h3><p>El equipo de Data y Analytics trabaja en diferentes proyectos que combinan volúmenes de datos enormes e IA, como detectar y predecir fallas antes que ocurran, optimizar pricing, personalizar la experiencia del cliente, optimizar uso de combustible, detectar caras y objetos usando visión por computador.</p><p>Como DevOps Engineer, tu trabajo es clave en construir y proveer los sistemas e infraestructura que permiten el desarrollo de estos servicios, formando los cimientos sobre los cuales las y los Software Engineers construyen los modelos que permiten generar impacto, con servicios que deben escalar, con altísima disponibilidad y tolerantes a fallas, en otras palabras, que funcionen. Además, mantendrás tu mirada en los indicadores de capacidad y performance de los sistemas.</p><p>En cualquier proyecto que trabajes, esperamos que tengas un gran espíritu de colaboración, una pasión por la innovación y el código y una mentalidad de automatización antes que procesos manuales.</p><p>Trabajarás en conjunto con ML Engineers, Data Scientists, Data Engineers, DevOps y Software Engineers. Cómo DevOps Engineer, tu trabajo consistirá en:</p><ul><li>Participar activamente durante el ciclo de vida del software, desde inception, diseño, deploy, operación y mejora.</li><li>Apoyar a los equipos de desarrollo en actividades de diseño y consultoría, desarrollando software, frameworks y capacity planning.</li><li>Manejar y monitorear el desempeño de infraestructura y aplicaciones.</li><li>Poner en práctica conceptos de Site Reliability Engineering cómo SLA, SLI, SLO, error budgets, entre otros, con métricas de confiabilidad y performance adecuadas a cada modelo.</li><li>Asegurar la escalabilidad y resiliencia.</li><li>Promover buenas prácticas en desarrollo de software, fomentando la automatización y monitoreo continuo.</li></ul><h3>Deseable</h3><ul><li>Agilidad para visualizar posibles mejoras, problemas y soluciones en Arquitecturas.</li><li>Entendimiento de arquitectura de microservicios y orquestación de containers con Kubernetes.</li><li>Conocimiento de elementos de SRE y MLOps (CT).</li><li>Experiencia en la construcción y optimización de pipelines de producción e infraestructura como código.</li></ul><h3>Beneficios</h3><ul><li>Bono por desempeño</li><li>Bono de almuerzo mensual y almuerzo de equipo</li><li>Seguro Complementario de salud y dental</li><li>Horario flexible</li><li>Flexibilidad entre oficina y home office</li><li>Medio día libre el día de tu cumpleaños</li><li>Financiamiento de certificaciones</li><li>Inscripción en Coursera con plan de entrenamiento a medida</li><li>Estacionamiento de bicicletas</li><li>Programa de referidos</li><li>Salida de “teambuilding” mensual</li></ul>' WHERE url_vacante=N'https://www.getonbrd.com/jobs/devops-engineer-neuralworks-santiago-219c' AND fuente_id IN (SELECT fuente_id FROM dbo.dim_fuente WHERE nombre='GetOnBoard');
