UPDATE dbo.fact_vacantes SET titulo=N'Sr. Java Platform Engineer', descripcion=N'<h3>Must Have</h3><ul><li><strong>Java 11+:</strong> strong hands-on development experience.</li><li><strong>Terraform:</strong> real, practical infrastructure-as-code experience (not just familiarity).</li><li><strong>Security frameworks and authentication mechanisms:</strong> hands-on experience implementing security controls and authentication mechanisms.</li><li><strong>Cloud platform experience:</strong> deep experience deploying and scaling cloud-based systems.</li><li><strong>Core platform systems:</strong> experience building and supporting core platform systems in production environments.</li></ul><div><strong>Ideal profile / what success looks like:</strong> we are looking for a Software/Platform Engineer who has evolved from software development into cloud infrastructure and platform engineering. You should be able to reason about security, scalability, and maintainability—and translate those concerns into platform and infrastructure code.</div><div><strong>Soft skills we value:</strong> we expect clear communication, ownership, and strong collaboration with other engineers and client stakeholders. We also value an engineering mindset focused on quality, continuous improvement, and pragmatic decision-making.</div><h3>Funciones</h3><div>We need a Software/Platform Engineer who combines strong Java engineering with real cloud infrastructure and platform work. You will be responsible for building, operating, and improving core platform systems that support our client’s cloud environments.</div><ul><li>Implement and maintain platform security controls and authentication mechanisms across the platform.</li><li>Develop infrastructure code for cloud deployments and scaling using Infrastructure-as-Code practices.</li><li>Build, support, and evolve core platform systems that enable platform reliability and developer productivity.</li><li>Contribute to platform hardening and operational readiness, ensuring secure-by-design workflows.</li><li>Collaborate with client stakeholders and internal teams to understand requirements and translate them into maintainable platform capabilities.</li><li>Perform other responsibilities as directed by the client, aligned with platform engineering needs.</li></ul><div><strong>How we think about the work:</strong> this is not a traditional DevOps role. We want someone who can design and implement platform software and infrastructure together—turning Java expertise into scalable, secure cloud platform outcomes.</div><h3>Deseable</h3><ul><li>Apache Arrow.</li><li>Kubernetes or other container orchestration experience.</li><li>CI/CD pipeline experience.</li></ul><div>These strengths help us accelerate delivery of platform capabilities, improve deployment workflows, and support modern data and infrastructure patterns.</div><h3>Beneficios</h3><ul><li>Contrato a largo plazo.</li><li>100% Remoto.</li><li>Vacaciones y PTOs.</li><li>Posibilidad de recibir 2 bonos al año.</li><li>2 revisiones salariales al año.</li><li>Clases de inglés.</li><li>Equipamiento Apple.</li><li>Plataforma de cursos en linea.</li><li>Budget para compra de libros.</li><li>Budget para compra de materiales de trabajo.</li><li>Mucho más.</li></ul><div>We foster teamwork, excellence, and fun—an environment that supports joy, open communication, personal growth, and shared rewards. If this Platform Engineer role matches your profile, we encourage you to apply.</div>' WHERE url_vacante=N'https://www.getonbrd.com/jobs/sr-java-platform-engineer-improving-remote' AND fuente_id IN (SELECT fuente_id FROM dbo.dim_fuente WHERE nombre='GetOnBoard');
