UPDATE dbo.fact_vacantes SET titulo=N'AI Product Experience Designer', descripcion=N'<h3>Requerimientos del cargo</h3><p><strong>3+ years in a role built around synthesis and structured thinking</strong> — strategy consulting, an internal strategy/insights function, or a closely comparable background where the core skill was turning large amounts of complex information into a clear recommendation.</p><p><strong>Demonstrated hands-on experience building with AI tools</strong> — not just using ChatGPT day-to-day, but having actually shipped something (an internal tool, a prototype, a side project) using tools like Claude Code, Cursor, v0, Lovable, or similar. Be ready to show it, not just describe it.</p><p><strong>Fluent written and spoken English and Spanish.</strong></p><p><strong>Based in Latin America</strong>, with the flexibility to work in real time with a team spanning Argentina and Uruguay.</p><p><strong>Comfortable working without a fully defined brief.</strong> This role is inherently ambiguous at the start — the ability to bring structure to an undefined problem is part of the job, not a gap to fill in later.</p><h3>Funciones</h3><p><strong>Area:</strong> Product Experience — sits between product architecture, creative direction, and engineering.</p><p><strong>Core function:</strong> Decide how the intelligence Growth Signal generates gets experienced by the customer — what''s communicated, in what order, and at what level of detail.</p><p><strong>Responsibilities:</strong></p><ul><li>Take AI-assembled insights, reports, and data modules and shape them into a clear narrative — deciding what''s the headline, what comes first, and what deserves deeper explanation.</li><li>Decide what to leave out. Not every insight needs to be shown; part of the job is protecting the customer from noise.</li><li>Design the sequence and structure of customer-facing experiences: reports, dashboards, onboarding flows, and lifecycle communications.</li><li>Determine how to build trust in what''s being shown — what level of detail, transparency, or explanation makes an insight credible rather than just accurate.</li><li>Prototype directly using AI-native tools (Claude Code, Cursor, v0, Lovable, or similar) rather than handing off static specs — you take ideas from concept to something testable yourself.</li><li>Partner closely with Nani (product architecture) and Pedro (creative direction) to keep the underlying structure, visual language, and narrative coherent with each other — this is a shared loop, not a solo handoff.</li><li>Work directly alongside engineering to test and iterate on real product experiences, not mockups that sit and wait for review.</li><li>Help define and evolve a consistent experience language across every Force of Nature product over time.</li></ul><p><strong>What this role does not do:</strong> own or redesign the underlying product/data architecture (that stays with Nani), or produce static design deliverables disconnected from a working prototype.</p><h3>Deseable</h3><h3>Beneficios</h3><p>This role offers ongoing freelance engagement with a remote-first team in South America. Shortlisted applicants may complete a paid design exercise using a real Force of Nature use case to demonstrate data-to-visual storytelling capabilities.</p>' WHERE url_vacante=N'https://www.getonbrd.com/jobs/editor-of-customer-experience-product-narrative-strategy-force-of-nature-remote' AND fuente_id IN (SELECT fuente_id FROM dbo.dim_fuente WHERE nombre='GetOnBoard');
