UPDATE dbo.fact_vacantes SET titulo=N'Data/Software Engineer (Sas→Python)', descripcion=N'<h3>Required both:</h3><ul><li>4+ years of professional data or software engineering experience.</li><li>Strong Python and SQL.</li><li>Hands-on Databricks experience, including <strong>Unity Catalog</strong>, <strong>Workflows</strong>, and <strong>Databricks Asset Bundles</strong>.</li><li>GitLab CI/CD experience: pipelines, merge request workflows, and automated testing.</li><li>Git branching and code review discipline.</li><li>Clear written and spoken English for client-facing collaboration with partners.</li><li>Demonstrated ownership: scoping, delivering, and flagging risk without prompting.</li></ul><p><strong>We’re looking for someone who can ensure the reliability of converted pipelines</strong>—not only writing code, but also validating results and operating deployments responsibly. You should be comfortable investigating failures, improving performance, and maintaining high standards for correctness and reproducibility in a collaborative environment.</p><h3>Funciones</h3><p><strong>Pipeline reliability, validation, and delivery of converted code.</strong></p><ul><li>Build and run the pipelines that process SAS inventories and converted outputs.</li><li>Validate converted code for parity against SAS outputs (row counts, checksums, schema, data types).</li><li>Own deployment through Databricks Asset Bundles (DABs) and GitLab CI/CD.</li><li>Manage Unity Catalog objects, permissions, and environment promotion.</li><li>Troubleshoot job failures and performance issues.</li><li>Perform <strong>Spark</strong> and <strong>Delta Lake</strong> performance tuning.</li><li>Apply data validation and reconciliation practices to ensure correctness.</li><li>Use <strong>Infrastructure as Code</strong> or DAB-based deployment approaches.</li></ul><p>You’ll also communicate directly with client and partner stakeholders and coordinate deliverables with clear ownership from scoping through delivery, including proactive risk flagging.</p><h3>Deseable</h3><ul><li>Ability to read SAS.</li><li>Healthcare data exposure.</li><li>Azure experience.</li></ul><p>Any experience that helps you quickly understand legacy SAS logic, map it to Python/SQL equivalents, and collaborate across environments will be a plus.</p><h3>Beneficios</h3><ul><li>Contrato a largo plazo.</li><li>100% Remoto.</li><li>Vacaciones y PTOs.</li><li>Posibilidad de recibir 2 bonos al año.</li><li>2 revisiones salariales al año.</li><li>Clases de inglés.</li><li>Equipamiento Apple.</li><li>Plataforma de cursos en linea.</li><li>Budget para compra de libros.</li><li>Budget para compra de materiales de trabajo.</li><li>Mucho más..</li></ul>' WHERE url_vacante=N'https://www.getonbrd.com/jobs/data-software-engineer-sas-python-improving-remote' AND fuente_id IN (SELECT fuente_id FROM dbo.dim_fuente WHERE nombre='GetOnBoard');
