UPDATE dbo.fact_vacantes SET titulo=N'Head of SEO — Medical Accounts', descripcion=N'<h3>Requirements:</h3><ul><li>Available 9:00 AM to 5:00 PM US Eastern, Monday to Friday. This schedule is fixed - our clients are American and you will be on their calls. Please check what that means where you live before applying.</li><li>Fluent in the stack: Screaming Frog or an equivalent crawler, Google Search Console, GA4, Ahrefs or Semrush, WordPress at agency scale, Google Business Profile, and structured data.</li><li>Managed at least two people for at least a year — actually managed them, including telling someone their work wasn''t good enough and keeping them on the team afterwards</li><li>Have been the accountable person for a domain''s organic performance, not a contributor to it</li><li>Can hold a 45-minute call in English with a physician-owner who interrupts you, without a script. Advanced English (C1+) is a hard requirement, not a preference</li><li>Technical SEO deep enough to explain a Core Web Vitals fix in terms of the asset causing it, read a log file when the crawl summary doesn''t add up, and refuse a quick fix that breaks something downstream</li><li>Understand why medical content needs a reviewer, and what happens to a practice that publishes treatment claims without one</li></ul><p>Not a fit if: you want strategy without hands-on technical work · you don''t want to be on client calls · your management experience is "mentoring juniors" · you need the agenda sent to you before you know what to prepare · you''d rather your boss delivered the hard message to your team member · you''ve bought links or published unreviewed AI content for a medical client and thought it was fine</p><h3>Funciones</h3><ul><li>The technical standard across every account — crawl health, indexation, schema, Core Web Vitals, migrations, and the judgment calls above them</li><li>The client relationship. You run the recurring SEO calls yourself: set the agenda, present results, defend the plan when a client pushes back, and say no when what they want will hurt them</li><li>A team of junior SEO specialists. You assign their work, review it before it ships, and tell them directly when it isn''t good enough</li><li>Coverage. Every account has a named backup with real context, so a week of your absence moves nothing</li></ul><p><strong>Your first 90 days</strong></p><p>You take over the recurring client calls. You publish an account plan and a call agenda before each one, not after. You put a QA gate in front of everything the juniors ship. You build the backup map. By day 90, nothing in the department waits on you personally to unblock it.</p><h3>Deseable</h3><p>Experience with medical, dental, legal or other regulated/YMYL accounts<br>• Google Business Profile and multi-location local SEO<br>• WordPress at agency scale<br>• Experience building a junior team from scratch, not just inheriting one<br>• Familiarity with AI-assisted SEO workflows and AI search visibility<br>• Bilingual Spanish/English — our team spans several countries</p><h3>Beneficios</h3><ul><li>USD compensation paid via Wise, on the 15th and last day of each month</li><li>A written 90-day review against a defined scorecard, with a raise attached to it</li><li>Full ownership of the SEO department - you set the standard rather than inherit someone else''s</li><li>A junior team to build and lead, with real hiring input</li><li>A direct working relationship with the founder. No layers, no politics</li><li>Fixed hours and no on-call. When your day ends, it ends</li></ul>' WHERE url_vacante=N'https://www.getonbrd.com/jobs/head-of-seo-medical-accounts-tier3-media-remote' AND fuente_id IN (SELECT fuente_id FROM dbo.dim_fuente WHERE nombre='GetOnBoard');
