UPDATE dbo.fact_vacantes SET titulo=N'Technical Lead (Back-end Hubspot Integrations & Migrations)', descripcion=N'<h3>What you bring</h3><p>We expect you to bring strong backend engineering skills and proven leadership experience in delivery. You’ll work directly with our team on HubSpot API-driven solutions and take responsibility for end-to-end outcomes—from technical design through tested releases.</p><ul><li><strong>Years</strong> of backend development using Node.js, Python, PHP, or similar technologies.</li><li><strong>Hands-on HubSpot experience</strong> with the API, integrations, or migration projects.</li><li><strong>Leadership</strong>: experience leading developers and managing projects end to end (planning, execution, quality, and delivery).</li><li><strong>Communication</strong>: fluent in<strong> English</strong>, with the ability to explain technical status in plain language.</li><li><strong>Collaboration &amp; time zone fit</strong>: Daily overlap with <strong>US Eastern</strong> business hours.</li><li><strong>Quality mindset</strong>: you take testing seriously and ensure releases are safe, documented, and approved.</li></ul><p>We also value practical ownership and calm execution: you keep teams aligned, make progress visible, and handle technical trade-offs with clarity.</p><h3>Funciones</h3><p>We’re looking for a HubSpot Technical Lead who can both lead and build. You’ll guide a small team of developers delivering HubSpot integrations, migrations, and custom builds while also working hands-on on backend services.</p><ul><li>Lead a small team of developers working on HubSpot integrations, migrations, and custom builds.</li><li>Plan delivery: define work for each project, assign tasks, and confirm hours weekly.</li><li>Own scheduling and delivery momentum, keeping work on track and surfacing risks early.</li><li>Guarantee quality: run QA and ensure nothing goes live until it’s tested and signed off.</li><li>Write and review backend code, APIs, and data migration logic yourself.</li><li>Act as the technical point of contact for clients, translating progress into clear, plain-language updates.</li><li>Coordinate technical decisions across the team to keep implementations consistent and maintainable.</li></ul><h3>Deseable</h3><ul><li><p>Experience with data migration strategies for CRMs (validation, reconciliation, rollback planning, and post-migration checks).</p></li><li><p>Working knowledge of API design, authentication patterns, rate limits, and webhook/event-driven integrations.</p></li><li><p>Familiarity with CI/CD workflows, automated testing, and code review processes in a production environment.</p></li><li><p>Experience partnering with client stakeholders to translate requirements into engineering deliverables.</p></li></ul><h3>Beneficios</h3><ul><li><strong>Fully remote.</strong> Work from anywhere, with a team spread across several countries.</li><li><strong>Paid time off.</strong> Company holidays and year-end closure.</li><li><strong>Employee Assistance Program.</strong> Confidential financial and mental health support.</li><li><strong>Real leadership.</strong> You lead the development team and own delivery from start to finish, instead of being one developer among many.</li><li><strong>HubSpot Elite Solutions Partner.</strong> You work on enterprise HubSpot projects with complex integrations, migrations and custom builds.</li><li><strong>International clients</strong> in North America, the UK and Europe, and Australia and Asia-Pacific.</li><li><strong>Continuous learning support.</strong> Access to Udemy, plus financial grants for further education where relevant to your role.</li><li><strong>Room to grow.</strong> A lean team where strong delivery is noticed and rewarded.</li></ul>' WHERE url_vacante=N'https://www.getonbrd.com/jobs/technical-lead-backend-hubspot-integrations-migrations-wendt-partners-remote' AND fuente_id IN (SELECT fuente_id FROM dbo.dim_fuente WHERE nombre='GetOnBoard');
