UPDATE dbo.fact_vacantes SET titulo=N'Senior Forward Deployed Engineer', descripcion=N'<h3>Requerimientos del cargo</h3><div>- 5+ years of software engineering or integration engineering experience.<br>- C1 English level or higher.<br>- Demonstrated experience building or deploying agentic AI systems that select tools, plan and execute multi-step tasks.<br>- Working knowledge of Model Context Protocol (MCP) or equivalent production tool-orchestration frameworks.<br>- Solid experience with enterprise integration patterns: APIs, ETL/ELT, data pipelines, middleware and event-driven architectures.<br>- Proven experience navigating enterprise infosec reviews and data governance requirements.<br>- Strong customer-facing communication; able to explain technical concepts to non-technical operators.<br>- Comfortable working autonomously with minimal supervision inside a customer''s environment.<br>- Experience with AI-first development practices (AI-assisted development, AI-generated testing, agent-based workflows).<br>- Able to travel to the U.S. on short notice for up to two weeks, with a valid B1/B2 visa or ESTA eligibility already in place.</div><h3>Funciones</h3><p>As a Senior Forward Deployed Engineer, you will lead the technical integration of the platform directly into customer environments. You will:<br>- Lead integration projects inside customer environments, connecting the platform to the systems the operator already runs.<br>- Map customer operational workflows and translate them into platform configurations, data models and automated integrations.<br>- Build and maintain production agentic AI systems using Model Context Protocol (MCP) to manage tools, context and memory.<br>- Own onboarding acceleration: configuration, data migration and ingestion pipelines.<br>- Guide deployments through customer IT and cybersecurity reviews.<br>- Serve as the named technical contact for assigned accounts.<br>- Identify repeatable integration patterns and turn them into productization candidates for the core engineering team.<br>This is a remote role based in LATAM with required travel: expect periodic trips to customer sites in the U.S. of up to two weeks at a time, sometimes as the sole company representative on site.</p><h3>Deseable</h3><div>- Enterprise ERP or property management system (PMS) integration experience.<br>- Prior customer-facing engineering role (Solutions Architect, Implementation Engineer, Technical Account Manager).<br>- Background in real estate operations, self-storage or PropTech.<br>- Experience in small, empowered teams (1–4 people) owning the full development lifecycle with AI agents.</div><h3>Beneficios</h3><p>Remote from LATAM (full-time contracting), with required periodic travel to customer sites in the U.S. (up to 2 weeks per trip).</p><div>Niuro supports a 100% remote work model, allowing flexibility in work location globally. We invest in career development through ongoing training programs and leadership opportunities, ensuring continuous growth and success.</div><div>Upon successful completion of the initial contract, there is potential for long-term collaboration and stable, full-time employment, reflecting our long-term commitment to our team members.</div><div>Joining Niuro means becoming part of a global community dedicated to technological excellence and benefiting from a strong administrative support infrastructure that enables you to focus on impactful work without distraction.</div>' WHERE url_vacante=N'https://www.getonbrd.com/jobs/forward-deployed-engineer-niuro-remote-87ec' AND fuente_id IN (SELECT fuente_id FROM dbo.dim_fuente WHERE nombre='GetOnBoard');
