UPDATE dbo.fact_vacantes SET titulo=N'Director of Operations', descripcion=N'<h3>WHAT WE’RE LOOKING FOR</h3><p>Must have:</p><ul><li>5+ years running operations in a professional services, advisory, private equity, or law firm environment</li><li>Chief of staff, director of operations, practice manager, or business manager</li><li>Direct experience running an operating cadence (EOS/Traction, 4DX, OKRs, or a homegrown equivalent).</li><li>Documentation and process discipline</li><li>Working command of a deal or relationship CRM and comfort administering data standards</li><li>U.S. Eastern time or a good portion of your hours aligned with our working time zone.</li></ul><p>Helpful, not required:</p><ul><li>Law firm or legal services operations background</li><li>Exposure to M&amp;A transaction process, deal desk, or contract administration</li><li>Experience inside a partner-led business</li></ul><p><strong>WHO THIS ROLE ISN’T FOR</strong></p><ul><li>If you want to redesign the operating system rather than run it week after week, you will be bored here.</li><li>If you disengage when people don’t comply and let the system do the confronting for you, this role will fail.</li><li>If the appeal is a path into origination or deal execution, that is not on offer.</li><li>If a job whose central function is enforcing consistency sounds tedious to you, trust that instinct.</li></ul><h3>Funciones</h3><ol><li>The operating cadence. - Leadership and department meetings ran, held, and recorded. Agendas distributed, scorecards fully populated before and every assigned task and priority tied to a company initiative and quarterly goal.</li><li>Pipeline operations integrity. - CRM hygiene and stage velocity as a managed system: a current interaction logged on every active deal, stage violations surfaced automatically, and stale inventory driven down.</li><li>Team coordination and capacity protection. - Task closure tracked and enforced. Capacity limits are accessed and honored. No critical function left with a single point of failure and no backup. We’re building to scale and you’ll be responsible for redundancy implementation.</li><li>Leadership optimization - Every new “yes” logged alongside the “no” it displaces. Priority changes announced in the room and rather than absorbed quietly. A monthly compliance report that lands on the founders’ desks without anyone asking for it.</li></ol><h3>Deseable</h3><h3>Beneficios</h3>' WHERE url_vacante=N'https://www.getonbrd.com/jobs/director-of-operations-exitpath-partners-llc-remote' AND fuente_id IN (SELECT fuente_id FROM dbo.dim_fuente WHERE nombre='GetOnBoard');
DELETE e FROM dbo.cert_evidencia_v2 e JOIN dbo.fact_vacantes v ON v.vacante_id=e.vacante_id WHERE url_vacante=N'https://www.getonbrd.com/jobs/director-of-operations-exitpath-partners-llc-remote' AND fuente_id IN (SELECT fuente_id FROM dbo.dim_fuente WHERE nombre='GetOnBoard');
UPDATE dbo.fact_vacantes SET titulo=N'Merch Designer', descripcion=N'<h3>You are a fit if you have</h3><div>You have the creative and production instincts to make merchandise concepts feel real, persuasive, and shippable. You can read a rough brief, ask a couple of strong questions, and return polished decks and visuals that move the sale forward.</div><ul><li><strong>Portfolio strength:</strong> a portfolio heavy on merchandise, apparel, or product concepting, plus persuasive pitch or sales decks.</li><li><strong>Production instincts:</strong> you understand how creative choices translate to real-world execution—knowing when a design needs one color instead of four, what embroidery can and can’t do, and where a print sits on a garment.</li><li><strong>Tool mastery:</strong> strong command of <strong>Figma</strong> and <strong>Adobe</strong> (Illustrator, Photoshop, InDesign).</li><li><strong>AI fluency:</strong> comfortable using AI image tools for mockups and concepting to accelerate quality and iteration.</li><li><strong>Communication:</strong> strong written and spoken English, with the ability to present concepts clearly and confidently.</li><li><strong>Speed &amp; self-direction:</strong> you operate with urgency and clarity—turning a brief into finished concepts quickly, then responding to two structured feedback checkpoints.</li></ul><div>We also value calm collaboration. You’re proactive about asking two good questions upfront, you respect feedback structure, and you help keep projects moving when priorities change due to client direction.</div><h3>Funciones</h3><div>You turn a brief into a pitch that closes. A client comes to us with a logo, a moment, and a budget. We expect you to come back with a curated product story, mockups that look real, and a deck built inside their brand world. Your work is the bridge between early direction and the final creative direction that the client can confidently say yes to.</div><ul><li>Build client pitch decks, from our company overview through bespoke project decks per client—using their tone, style, and brand look and feel.</li><li>Create product mockups and concept visuals that communicate the value clearly and help clients want the thing before it exists.</li><li>Own product curation with the account team: selecting the right items, colors, and decoration methods for each brand and use case.</li><li>Translate founder and account team direction into finished concepts fast—typically with one round of revisions, not repeated rework.</li><li>Coordinate your output with our process: you take a written brief, receive feedback at two fixed checkpoints (concept and final), and adjust priorities when a client’s direction shifts—without reopening finished work unless a new brief is issued.</li></ul><h3>Deseable</h3><ul><li>Experience collaborating directly with account teams or founders to translate client goals into presentation-ready creative.</li><li>Familiarity with common merchandise decoration techniques and constraints (e.g., embroidery, screen printing, heat transfer) and how they influence mockups.</li><li>Comfort presenting concepts in a way that balances creativity with commercial clarity (cost-awareness, feasibility, and brand alignment).</li><li>Demonstrated ability to build cohesive deck narratives quickly—company overview to bespoke project story—without losing design craft.</li></ul><h3>Beneficios</h3><div>Work with fast-growing, brand-conscious clients who care about doing swag right. Blend creativity (gifting, product, design) with strategy (accounts, growth, margin). Join a small, agile team where your ideas and relationships can make a real impact. We provide a collaborative environment, opportunities for career growth, and the chance to shape premier gifting programs for leading brands.</div>' WHERE url_vacante=N'https://www.getonbrd.com/jobs/creative-account-manager-better-swag-remote' AND fuente_id IN (SELECT fuente_id FROM dbo.dim_fuente WHERE nombre='GetOnBoard');
